## ANTI-PATTERNS (LEARNED FROM PRIOR BRIEFS)

Do not do these. They have caused real bugs.

### Do not call `awardEssence` when the Pool update needs to fire later than t=0
The Pool update has a specific timing in ceremony sequences. Calling `awardEssence` at the wrong moment breaks the ceremony pacing.

### Do not assume pregame function names exist in atheneum
The two files have different naming conventions and different function inventories. Verify the function exists in atheneum before referencing it.

### Do not use `setInnerHTML` on elements with active animations
Wipes the animation state mid-frame. Use append/replaceChild patterns instead.

### Do not silently expand scope to "fix something while I'm in there"
Surface the related issue. Let the chat decide whether to scope a follow-on brief.

### Do not report "shipped" when only compilation verified
Run the code. Load the page. Capture artifacts. Then report.

### Do not pick names for new mechanics, chambers, or concepts
Names are operator decisions made through Architecture & Decisions chat. If a brief asks for naming, surface it as a design question and halt.

