## CACHE AND RELOAD DISCIPLINE

When verifying changes in browser:
- Hard reload (Ctrl+Shift+R or Cmd+Shift+R) to bypass cache
- Verify the new code is actually running (check console log, check element existence, check class names)
- If state seems stale, clear `localStorage` and reload to test from clean state
- Use `devReset` or similar dev controls when available rather than hand-clearing localStorage

---

## DEV CONTROLS (ATHENEUM)

Available at `window.atheneum.*` in the browser console:
- `devUnlockAll` — unlocks all modules
- `devCompletePage` — completes current sub-unit
- `devTriggerBronze` — re-fires Anchored ceremony
- `devSimulateDive` — runs the dive sequence
- `devReplayWelcome` — replays welcome moment
- `devClearVideo` — clears CTA video state
- `devReset` — clears state and reloads
- `devCompleteAllRetrievals` — fast-forwards retrievals (Brief 6 addition)
- `userState()` — dumps current state
- `CONSTELLATIONS()` — surfaces constellation data

Use these for verification rather than hand-manipulating state.

