## HONEST LIMITATIONS

If you cannot complete a brief as specified, say so explicitly. Do not partially complete and report shipped. Do not work around the constraint silently.

Examples:
- "I cannot run the code in this environment. Operator verification required at Layer 3 before this can be considered shipped."
- "The brief assumes function X exists; it doesn't. Halting for chat to either update the brief or scope a precursor brief."
- "Voice canon scan flagged 3 banned phrases in the brief's drafted copy. Halting before applying. Operator review needed."

Halted honestly beats shipped broken.

